## Domain Synthesis (compressed from verified file §3 Aggregate Finding + XC-11 architecture)

**What this domain establishes.** D4 documents the federal/state/local mandate-stack architecture governing FDA-regulated products (food, drugs, biologics, devices, cosmetics, tobacco) plus USDA-regulated meat and poultry plus DEA-regulated controlled substances serving PA-3, with primary institutional embodiment at the **FDA Philadelphia District** (Mellon Independence Center, 900 US Customhouse, 2nd & Chestnut, Philadelphia 19106), the **PDPH Office of Food Protection** (1101 Market Street), the **Pennsylvania Department of Agriculture (PADA) Bureau of Food Safety and Laboratory Services**, the **Pennsylvania Department of Human Services (PADHS)** for SNAP administration, and the **DEA Philadelphia Field Division**.

**The aggregate finding.** The federal product-regulatory architecture is nominally comprehensive across all six substantive sub-domains (food, meat &amp; poultry, drugs, biologics &amp; devices, tobacco, controlled substances), but in 2025-2026 the federal capacity to operate it has eroded through three documented co-occurring patterns: **(1) rule-availability erosion** — January 21, 2025 menthol cigarette ban + cigar characterizing flavors rule withdrawals (MC-V-6); April 25, 2025 Salmonella framework withdrawal + December 2025 NRTE indefinite delay (MC-V-3); MoCRA implementation lag through 2026-2028. **(2) federal capacity erosion** — April 1, 2025 FDA RIF affecting ~3,500 personnel = 19% of workforce; CDER lost ~1,000 over three months; CDRH ~260 fired; CTP Office of Regulations "rendered effectively non-functional"; April 2025 USDA workforce reductions (11,300+ deferred resignations) (MC-V-7). **(3) data-infrastructure rollback** — USDA ERS Household Food Security report series terminated September 20, 2025 with the 2024 edition (MC-V-8); CDC FoodNet PA-3 disaggregation absence. The three patterns are documented as co-occurring through separate decisions, not inferred as a coordinated program (per XC-9 confabulation guard). The structural consequence is that the federal D4 architecture's capacity to identify, respond to, and remediate disparate-impact patterns at PA-3 sub-area level operates within a narrowing capacity envelope at exactly the moment when the documented compound-disadvantage geography concentrates the patterns the architecture would address.

**XC-11 — Independent / small organization compliance + access asymmetry as cross-cutting finding.** Across all sub-domains, small / independent / Black-owned organizations carry compliance-and-access burden differentials vs. corporate-chain organizations: small / Black-owned cosmetics manufacturers under MoCRA exemption thresholds (SD1); small carnicerías and small ethnic-market retail at Title 6 §6-300 + §6-301 jurisdictional interface (SD1/SD2); independent pharmacies post-Rite-Aid bankruptcy (SD3); small tobacco retailers under PA Clean Indoor Air Act preemption (SD5); small / Black-owned cell and gene therapy access at Penn/CHOP institutional level (SD4 Philadelphia paradox). The XC-11 framing names a recurring structural feature without collapsing it into a single mechanism.

**Both/And designations at sub-domain level** (preserved without collapse): (1) **SD1 federal-architecture-comprehensive AND federal-capacity-eroding** — FFDCA / FSMA / DSHEA / MoCRA + SNAP / WIC / NSLP architecture is real AND April 2025 FDA RIF + USDA ERS termination simultaneously erode operational capacity. (2) **SD4 substantive cell-and-gene-therapy availability AND Philadelphia paradox low uptake** — Casgevy + Lyfgenia FDA-approved with ~90% reimbursed access AND total US uptake ~164 cumulative through 2025 confirms low-uptake framing. (3) **SD7 federal-floor-protections-stable AND federal-administrative-capacity-eroding** — FFDCA / CSA / FSPTCA / FMIA / PPIA statutory floors stable AND April 2025 RIF + Office-level decimation reduce operational capacity. The three Both/Ands hold simultaneously across the domain.

**Cross-domain integration as referenced context.** D2 Public Health substance-use cross-reference (SD6 controlled substances); D6 Environment environmental-contamination cross-reference (SD2 food-supply and SD6 environmental drug-exposure); D12 Safety Net SNAP/WIC/NSLP cross-reference at D12 SD3 (SD1 food assistance); D21 Healthcare Delivery pharmaceutical-access cross-reference at D21 SD3 (SD3 drugs); D9 Finance &amp; Taxation federal-fiscal-flow architecture. The five-dimensional anchor accountability framework (D7 + D9 + D8 + D10 + D6) completed at D6 verified file is referenced as established context; D4 intersects at federal-regulatory-architecture-erosion without extending.

